<===> README.md
Unlike `meta.load-css()`, errors that appear during CSS extension and
serialization aren't triggered just be loading a module with `meta.load()`.

<===>
================================================================================
<===> extend/input.scss
@use "sass:meta";
$_: meta.load("other");

<===> extend/_other.scss
a {@extend missing}

<===> extend/output.css

<===>
================================================================================
<===> serialize/input.scss
@use "sass:meta";
$_: meta.load("other");

<===> serialize/_other.scss
a {b: (c: d)}

<===> serialize/output.css
